{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1533217-supernatural-merits-and-mortal-magic","id":1533217,"title":"Supernatural Merits and Mortal Magic","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-03-26T16:57:39-07:00","id":1533217,"title":"Supernatural Merits and Mortal Magic","content":"How do you use Supernatural Merits in your games? How do you mechanically represent mortal occultists, psychics, shamans, and the like? How do you feel about the mechanics presented for Supernatural Merits? Do you prefer the current system, or the system of minor templates presented by Second Sight?<br /> <br /> This is intended to be a pretty general thread. Feel free to talk about how you run things in your games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28352-verlan","name":"Verlan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"118"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-26T17:24:16-07:00","id":1533220,"title":"","content":"I like both, though it was a bit of an adjustment coming from a WoD background and expecting my sorcerers to have special powers that others don't have access to like hedge magic paths. I'm still not sure I like CofD's approach better, both have their advantages.<br /> <br /> One thing I do think CofD does especially well that is relevant here is cults. I love how the cult merits work, especially with them being able to grant supernatural merits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27618,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","user":"ShadowcatX","date":". 03-26-2024, 08:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-26T17:44:33-07:00","id":1533223,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1533217-supernatural-merits-and-mortal-magic?p=1533220#post1533220\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like both, though it was a bit of an adjustment coming from a WoD background and expecting my sorcerers to have special powers that others don't have access to like hedge magic paths. I'm still not sure I like CofD's approach better, both have their advantages.<br /> <br /> One thing I do think CofD does especially well that is relevant here is cults. I love how the cult merits work, especially with them being able to grant supernatural merits.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I think both approaches have their merits. I feel like the main benefit to CofD's approach is that it lets you play mortal occultists using the core rulebook. It renders them feeling less like something extra that is grafted on and more like something that is an established part of the universe. On the other hand, it does not provide the sort of depth that a dedicated system for mortal magic could provide. I think your example with WoD is pretty pertinent. In CofD, you could manifest an occultist with a few Merits and Occult 4, whereas in OWoD you have a whole system dedicated to hedge magic. I feel like CofD's lighter system is more suited for games that primarily focus on mortals without supernatural powers, which was probably the intent. The dedicated systems presented in Second Sight feel more suited to a game where the party consists solely of thaumaturges or psychics.<br /> <br /> Also, it is interesting that you brought up the Mystery Cult Merits. I have never actually used them in my games, but the flavor is really good. The way progression of the Merit reflects further initiations is just cool. It is nice that they can grant Supernatural Merits, as you said.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28352-verlan","name":"Verlan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"118"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-26T18:03:53-07:00","id":1533224,"title":"","content":"If you want to see an example of a well done cult, Claire Redfield did a wonderful take on WoD's Pentex here: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/848028-mystery-cult-pentech-worldwide-leaders-in-natural-technology\">https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/...ral-technology</a><br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-27T12:57:47-07:00","id":1533268,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1533217-supernatural-merits-and-mortal-magic?p=1533224#post1533224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you want to see an example of a well done cult, Claire Redfield did a wonderful take on WoD's Pentex here: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/848028-mystery-cult-pentech-worldwide-leaders-in-natural-technology\">https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/...ral-technology</a><br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you for sharing that. I think that homebrew Mystery Cults are pretty rare.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28352-verlan","name":"Verlan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"118"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}